  "body": "Closes #122482\nRelated: #122194\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where direct OpenAI API-key users who selected cached WebSocket transport would reuse the socket but still resend the full conversation on each warm turn. Real provider output was rejected as changed history, so `previous_response_id` continuation never activated.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nContinuation matching now compares JSON values independently of object insertion order while preserving normal JSON omission semantics. At the assistant replay boundary, it removes only provider delivery metadata that reconstructed history cannot contain (`id`, `status`, `output_text.annotations`, and `output_text.logprobs`) while keeping semantic fields such as role, phase, text, reasoning shape, and tool-call data fail-closed.\n\nThe direct API-key default remains SSE. This PR does not add WebSocket preconnect/prewarm or the broader SSE continuation cache proposed in #122194.\n\nProduction LOC: +31/-14 (net +17) | Tests: +43/-7 (net +36) | Docs: +2/-2 (net 0)\n\n## User Impact\n\nExplicit `websocket-cached` and `auto` users on the built-in OpenAI Responses runtime now get the continuation behavior those modes promise: one session socket, `previous_response_id`, and suffix-only input when history is unchanged. Semantic history or request changes still invalidate continuation and send a full request.\n\nThe provider reference now accurately documents SSE as the direct API-key default and lists all supported explicit transport modes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Pre-fix production-path regression: a realistic completed OpenAI response with citation annotations, logprobs, and provider field order caused the second request to omit `previous_response_id`; the new regression fails on the old comparator and passes with this fix.\n- Focused exact-head tests: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/transports/openai-responses-websocket.test.ts packages/ai/src/transports/openai-responses-websocket-client.test.ts` -> 2 files, 29 tests passed.\n- Docs/static proof: full MDX check (770 files), docs/source formatting, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Changed-surface gate: core, coreTests, and docs passed locally after the remote Crabbox/Testbox backend was unavailable; core/test typechecks, lint, max-lines ratchet, deadcode, plugin boundaries, import cycles, schema and package guards were green.\n- Exact-head pull-request CI: [run 31569182042](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/31569182042) completed successfully on `dabe607efda854be74cc70e7432e19c321f15e6c`.\n- Authenticated live OpenAI A/B on the reviewed head: 48/48 complete; no WebSocket fallback, warning, or failure; cached WebSocket was the actual transport for 16/16 sequential turns; 12/12 warm turns reused the connection and continued with `previous_response_id`.\n- Warm sequential medians: first provider event 135.839 ms cached WebSocket vs 333 ms SSE; total duration 1082.076 ms vs 1109.844 ms; TTFT was comparable at 963.535 ms vs 920.231 ms, so this is a correctness/warm-start repair rather than a claim that WebSocket is universally faster.\n- Final Codex autoreview: clean; TruffleHog clean; patch correct 0.98.\n- Dependency contract review: latest sibling Codex typed continuation/suffix logic plus installed OpenAI SDK Responses WebSocket serialization and output types were inspected directly.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The implementation, proof, and final diff were reviewed by the maintainer.\n",
